{
  "_README": [
    "DISABLED. Activate with:  mv .mcp.json.disabled .mcp.json",
    "",
    "This does not work yet, and the blocker is not in this file.",
    "AIRTABLE_API_KEY is not registered in Infisical -- `lodge-doctor secret",
    "infisical-locator AIRTABLE_API_KEY` reports 'no active infisical secret",
    "found'. It currently exists only in the macOS keychain, which an agent",
    "process cannot read (rc=36, errSecInteractionNotAllowed).",
    "",
    "To enable:",
    "  1. Add AIRTABLE_API_KEY to Infisical (web UI).",
    "  2. Run /add-secret to register it in registry.yaml.",
    "  3. Verify:  GET_SECRET_DEBUG=1 get-secret.sh AIRTABLE_API_KEY >/dev/null",
    "  4. mv .mcp.json.disabled .mcp.json",
    "",
    "Why this resolves the secret through get-secret.sh rather than calling",
    "`security find-generic-password -w` directly, the way the parent pbswi",
    "workspace .mcp.json does: the raw keychain call is what the workspace",
    "convention explicitly forbids, and it is why AirTable access fails from",
    "every spawned agent process while appearing to work by hand.",
    "",
    "The wrapper fails loudly on purpose. A bare $(get-secret.sh ...) yields an",
    "EMPTY string when resolution fails, so the server would start cleanly and",
    "then 401 on every call -- a much worse failure than not starting."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "airtable": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "sh",
      "args": [
        "-c",
        "KEY=\"$(get-secret.sh AIRTABLE_API_KEY 2>/dev/null)\"; [ -n \"$KEY\" ] || { echo 'AIRTABLE_API_KEY did not resolve. Register it in Infisical, then run /add-secret. See .mcp.json.disabled for the full note.' >&2; exit 1; }; AIRTABLE_API_KEY=\"$KEY\" exec npx -y airtable-mcp-server"
      ]
    }
  }
}
